Note on the change: adding `complete_todo` required giving todos a "done" state, so I updated `add_todo` to store each item as `{"text": item, "done": False}` instead of the raw item — a plain string has nowhere to hold that state. `complete_todo` finds the first not-yet-done entry matching `item` and marks it done, raising `ValueError` if nothing matches (mirroring the `ValueError` pattern already used in `buggy.py`'s `divide`). Verified both functions interactively: add two todos, complete one, confirm only that one flips to `done: True`, and confirm completing a nonexistent item raises.

